---
code: records-fact-truncated
when-fires: fewer site records arrived than the header declared. plan/records.rs admit_records (the strict admission path); the forgiving deframer emits it too. `{received}`/`{declared}`/`{unseen}` are the site counts.
why: plans/128 fc-2 states the loss is bounded and computable against the declared count; the strict path refuses the attempt all the same (306b §6e), and the forgiving deframer keeps the count-only reading. NOTE plain-language pass owed: Unknown/⊤-join wording (law-plain-language-surfaces, 24H ack-4).
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork tune --profile web

-- probe-results.txt --
dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=6b796e0c816aa119a94373a3ab99578a69820f243017ce833973242dd6f9a79e sites=5 @@dorc@@
dorc site 0 effect=holds rc=0 @@dorc@@
dorc site 1 effect=holds rc=0 @@dorc@@
dorc site 2 effect=holds rc=0 @@dorc@@
dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --results - < probe-results.txt > /dev/null
records: note[records-fact-truncated]: the probe's records ended early: 3 of 5
declared site records arrived, so Dorc treats the 2 unseen site(s) as unanswered
and leaves their commands to run.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: records-fact-truncated
{{received}} = "3"
{{declared}} = "5"
{{unseen}} = "2"
